%N A271477 Total number of burnt pancakes flipped using the Max-bar(n) greedy algorithm.
%H A271477 Alois P. Heinz, <a href="/A271477/b271477.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..402</a> (first 128 terms from Gheorghe Coserea)
%H A271477 Richard E. Korf, <a href="https://cdn.aaai.org/AAAI/2008/AAAI08-050.pdf">Minimizing Disk I/O in Two-Bit Breadth-First Search</a>, In Proceedings of the 23rd AAAI Conf. on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI'08). AAAI Press, (2008), 317-324.
%H A271477 J. Sawada and A. Williams, <a href="https://www.cis.uoguelph.ca/~sawada/papers/pancake_successor.pdf">Successor rules for flipping pancakes and burnt pancakes</a>, Preprint, Theoretical Computer Science, Volume 609, Part 1, 4 January 2016, Pages 60-75.
%F A271477 a(n) = (n * 2^n * n!)/2 + Sum_{k=1..n-1} ((2*k + 1) * k * 2^k * k!)/2 for n >= 1. - _Paul Muljadi_, Oct 14 2026, after _Gheorghe Coserea_'s PARI code.
%o A271477 (PARI)
%o A271477 a(n) = n * 2^n * n!/2  + sum(k=1, n-1, (2*k+1) * k * 2^k * k!/2);
%o A271477 vector(20, k, a(k))  \\ _Gheorghe Coserea_, Apr 25 2016
%o A271477 (Python)
%o A271477 import math; print([n * 2**(n-1) * math.factorial(n) + sum((2*k+1) * k * 2**(k-1) * math.factorial(k) for k in range(1, n)) for n in range(1, 21)]) # _Paul Muljadi_, Oct 16 2026, after _Gheorghe Coserea_'s PARI code
